Selected frontend preparation shall bind four S-card terminals to a VSWITCH model, evaluate exactly one of each required scalar assignment in the model declaration's retained lexical environment, and preserve subcircuit port and parameter overrides. Unsupported model terms, other model families, instance parameters and missing/duplicate/unknown assignments shall refuse atomically. The motivating bug883 two-file circuit shall be compared against independent analytical and native ngspice output and control-excitation AC gains on both CPU providers, with compatibility mode and selected analyses recorded.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: InstanceBinder, DeclarationExtraction.HasOpaqueModelTerms, ParameterEvaluator lexical snapshot selection and OperatingPointBridge. Verification: PspiceSwitchTests, PspiceSwitchOracleIntegration and FrontendCorpusIntegration. Native original include uses ps mode; expanded-source selected OP/AC oracle uses explicit psa whole-deck conversion. Fixture provenance: https://sourceforge.net/p/ngspice/bugs/883/; no ngspice implementation code copied. The original native .99/1/1.01Hz sweep is separate from selected frontend1/100/1000Hz probes; Rust analytical tests cover original frequencies. High-impedance control differs from ngspice pswitch's default1TOhm input loading, irrelevant to the qualified ideal-control-source voltage outputs. Evidence: evidence/pspice-switch-results.json. Strict legacy Lower continues to refuse switch cards.
<<<
