STATEMENT: >>>
A retained two-to-four-field PULSE shall apply the native zero-delay and TSTEP rise defaults where appropriate and preserve the first rising segment and high hold through TSTOP. With both width and period defaulting to TSTOP, an equivalent PWL may represent the requested horizon. Explicit overlapping periodic fields and unrepresentable edge times shall refuse.
