[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-TRAN-DRIVEN-LTE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded adaptive integration of driven linear storage
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested transient analyses with a time-dependent source and linear capacitor or inductor storage shall use trapezoidal integration with local step-doubling error control when no method or trapezoidal order two is selected and initialization uses the ordinary operating point. The original maximum step and accepted-step ceiling shall be preserved, and the attempts ceiling shall be four times the accepted-step ceiling. An explicit first-order method shall retain its selected integration policy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
RequestedAnalysis supplies the existing Rust adaptive controller with relative tolerance 1e-7, absolute floors 1e-9 V and 1e-9 A, and minimum step equal to the larger of the smallest positive binary64 value and the step ceiling divided by one million. Verification uses RequestedAnalysisTests, original tests/general/rc.cir and the exact RC response. These local tolerances do not establish a global error bound or native trace agreement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-TRANSIENT-SELECT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-RESISTOR-AC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Distinct scalar resistance in requested small-signal analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
A scalar resistor with one AC assignment shall retain positive finite DC and AC resistances in ohms. Requested OP, DC and transient shall retain the DC resistance. Requested AC on a linear circuit shall use the AC resistance for that resistor without mutating the other requests. A requested AC circuit with bias-dependent elements shall refuse this profile until DC bias and AC conductance are supplied separately.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
PrimitiveExtraction retains the generated assignment, OperatingPointBridge binds both values in instance scope, and RequestedAnalysis projects the existing linear wire model for AC only. Reference behavior is ngspice resload.c and restemp.c. Evidence uses RequestedAnalysisTests and the two original res_partition paths.
